{
  "about": "The refusals of a specification's project function calls (FUNC-1, FUNC-4 to FUNC-6, COLUMN-4, COLUMN-6, NAME-3, LOOKUP-22), prepared in a project whose function files each define an integer identity, or prepared without a project, where each call misses its binding (CT-13), and a project's own scope findings: its names, sections, producers, cycles, saves and stale artifacts (PROJECT-5 to PROJECT-15). With `sources`, `prepare_in` reports what binding the prepared document to those schemas refuses. `called` derives VALUE with a call of the project function id, `nested` derives A with a call of the undeclared function unknown inside a case, and `mutual` derives A and B with calls of id that read each other. A case whose table compared part of a record compares those fields, and an `among` case finds its record by cause among the others.",
  "documents": {
